{"role":"assistant","content":"Диагноз по логам и коду (три независимых дефекта):\n\n1. **401 у всех**: «Connect» — обычная ссылка `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. Навигация браузера не несёт заголовок `Authorization` (его добавляет только fetch-обёртка), поэтому `require_user` отвечает 401 — ровно та белая страница из тикета #214.\n2. **400 invalid_request с 02.10**: в scope добавили `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. До релиза календаря (19.09 Ривера подключилась успешно) ссылка работала; удаление `state`/смена `redirect_uri` на ошибку не влияют — «мешает» именно scope. У Intervals.icu календарь — это «events», календарные scope называются `EVENT:READ`/`EVENT:WRITE`.\n3. **«Протухание» через час у Риверы**: Intervals не вернул ни `expires_in`, ни `refresh_token` (см. ответ токен-ендпоинта 19.09), а наш код при отсутствии `expires_in` выдумал TTL 3600 с и сам убил соединение.\n\nВношу исправления:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_1q5TKKMKY7u4IqOPlu21fqaJ","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"config.py\",\"old_string\":\"SCOPES = \\\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\\\"\",\"new_string\":\"SCOPES = \\\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,EVENT:READ,EVENT:WRITE\\\"\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_TQ8p8NvWdZKedctBs7lJ1SLI","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\",\"old_string\":\"AUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \\\"/oauth/authorize\\\"\\nDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\",\"new_string\":\"AUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \\\"/oauth/authorize\\\"\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_gP4xiD9MuzFiETm59hU43525","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\",\"old_string\":\"# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\",\"new_string\":\"# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\\n# expires_at=None means the provider reported no lifetime: the token does not expire.\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_P0r86mV2yZUZbfEoW87h6u5t","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\",\"old_string\":\"def store_connection(user_id, tok):\\n    expires_in = int(tok.get(\\\"expires_in\\\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\\n    refresh = tok.get(\\\"refresh_token\\\")\\n    if not refresh:\\n        log(f\\\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\\\")\\n    athlete = tok.get(\\\"athlete\\\") or {}\\n    with LOCK:\\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\\n            \\\"athlete_id\\\": athlete.get(\\\"id\\\"), \\\"athlete_name\\\": athlete.get(\\\"name\\\"),\\n            \\\"access_token\\\": tok[\\\"access_token\\\"], \\\"refresh_token\\\": refresh,\\n            \\\"scope\\\": tok.get(\\\"scope\\\"), \\\"expires_at\\\": time.time() + expires_in, \\\"status\\\": \\\"connected\\\",\\n        }\\n    log(f\\\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\\\")\",\"new_string\":\"def store_connection(user_id, tok):\\n    expires_in = tok.get(\\\"expires_in\\\")\\n    refresh = tok.get(\\\"refresh_token\\\")\\n    if not refresh:\\n        log(f\\\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response\\\")\\n    if not expires_in:\\n        log(f\\\"{user_id}: no expires_in in response, treating token as non-expiring\\\")\\n    athlete = tok.get(\\\"athlete\\\") or {}\\n    with LOCK:\\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\\n            \\\"athlete_id\\\": athlete.get(\\\"id\\\"), \\\"athlete_name\\\": athlete.get(\\\"name\\\"),\\n            \\\"access_token\\\": tok[\\\"access_token\\\"], \\\"refresh_token\\\": refresh,\\n            \\\"scope\\\": tok.get(\\\"scope\\\"),\\n            \\\"expires_at\\\": time.time() + int(expires_in) if expires_in else None,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"connected\\\",\\n        }\\n    log(f\\\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')}\\\"\\n        + (f\\\" (expires in {int(expires_in)}s)\\\" if expires_in else \\\" (no expiry reported)\\\"))\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_pIL5opczf8urmvp87jyDSsaw","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\",\"old_string\":\"        with LOCK:\\n            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\\n                if c[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"connected\\\" or c[\\\"expires_at\\\"] - now > 300:\\n                    continue\\n                if not c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"]:\\n                    log(f\\\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\\\")\\n                    c.update(status=\\\"expired, reconnect\\\", access_token=None)\\n                    continue\\n                try:\\n                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\\n                        \\\"grant_type\\\": \\\"refresh_token\\\", \\\"refresh_token\\\": c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"],\\n                        \\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID, \\\"client_secret\\\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\\n                    })\\n                    c.update(access_token=tok[\\\"access_token\\\"],\\n                             refresh_token=tok.get(\\\"refresh_token\\\", c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"]),\\n                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\\\"expires_in\\\"]))\\n                    log(f\\\"{uid}: token refreshed\\\")\",\"new_string\":\"        with LOCK:\\n            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\\n                if c[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"connected\\\":\\n                    continue\\n                if c[\\\"expires_at\\\"] is None or c[\\\"expires_at\\\"] - now > 300:\\n                    continue\\n                if not c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"]:\\n                    log(f\\\"{uid}: token expired and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\\\")\\n                    c.update(status=\\\"expired, reconnect\\\", access_token=None)\\n                    continue\\n                try:\\n                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\\n                        \\\"grant_type\\\": \\\"refresh_token\\\", \\\"refresh_token\\\": c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"],\\n                        \\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID, \\\"client_secret\\\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\\n                    })\\n                    new_exp = tok.get(\\\"expires_in\\\")\\n                    c.update(access_token=tok[\\\"access_token\\\"],\\n                             refresh_token=tok.get(\\\"refresh_token\\\", c[\\\"refresh_token\\\"]),\\n                             expires_at=now + int(new_exp) if new_exp else None)\\n                    log(f\\\"{uid}: token refreshed\\\")\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_5wux8a9NZyCq4m8KtOesHBGy","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\",\"old_string\":\"    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\\n    def auth_init(self):\\n        user = self.require_user()\\n        if not user:\\n            return\\n        params = {\\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID, \\\"redirect_uri\\\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\\n                  \\\"scope\\\": config.SCOPES, \\\"state\\\": sign_state(user[\\\"id\\\"])}\\n        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\\\":,\\\"))\",\"new_string\":\"    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and hand it to the SPA, which sends the\\n    # browser to Intervals. JSON (not a 302) so the SPA can fetch this with its\\n    # bearer token — a plain link would arrive here without Authorization.\\n    def auth_init(self):\\n        user = self.require_user()\\n        if not user:\\n            return\\n        params = {\\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID, \\\"response_type\\\": \\\"code\\\",\\n                  \\\"redirect_uri\\\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\\n                  \\\"scope\\\": config.SCOPES, \\\"state\\\": sign_state(user[\\\"id\\\"])}\\n        url = AUTHORIZE_URL + \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\\\":,\\\")\\n        self.send_json(200, {\\\"url\\\": url})\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_XUXg98ozBAi93BZLyl7dJWBR","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"static/app.js\",\"old_string\":\"      card = `<div class=\\\"card\\\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\\n        <p><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"/api/intervals/auth/init\\\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\\n    }\\n    root.className = \\\"\\\";\\n    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\\n    const d = document.getElementById(\\\"disconnect\\\");\\n    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\\\"/api/intervals/disconnect\\\", { method: \\\"POST\\\" }); render(); };\",\"new_string\":\"      card = `<div class=\\\"card\\\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\\n        <p><button class=\\\"btn\\\" id=\\\"connect\\\">Connect Intervals.icu</button></p></div>`;\\n    }\\n    root.className = \\\"\\\";\\n    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\\n    const d = document.getElementById(\\\"disconnect\\\");\\n    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\\\"/api/intervals/disconnect\\\", { method: \\\"POST\\\" }); render(); };\\n    const c = document.getElementById(\\\"connect\\\");\\n    if (c) c.onclick = async () => {\\n      c.disabled = true;\\n      try {\\n        const { url } = await api(\\\"/api/intervals/auth/init\\\");\\n        window.location.href = url;\\n      } catch (e) {\\n        c.disabled = false;\\n        root.innerHTML = `<p class=\\\"card\\\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\\n      }\\n    };\"}"}}]}
